SAVEPOINT f;
>>> EXPECTED ERROR [42501] the feed may not insert into price_ticks directly
INSERT INTO price_ticks (instrument_id, observed_at, price, source, source_event_id)
VALUES (6, now(), 100500, 'BINANCE', 'r2-feed-2');
psql:sql/review2/17_security.sql:192: ERROR:  permission denied for table price_ticks
<<< actual SQLSTATE: 42501
ROLLBACK TO SAVEPOINT f;
>>> EXPECTED ERROR [42501] the feed may not call ingest_tick by name (it needs table rights it does not have)
SELECT * FROM ingest_tick('BINANCE', 'BTCUSDT', '2026-10-13 10:07:26+05:30'::timestamptz + interval '1 second', 100510, 0.10, 'BINANCE', 'r2-feed-3');
psql:sql/review2/17_security.sql:196: ERROR:  permission denied for table instruments
CONTEXT:  SQL statement "SELECT i.instrument_id, i.is_active
                                          FROM instruments i
    WHERE i.exchange = p_exchange
      AND i.symbol   = p_symbol
    FOR NO KEY UPDATE"
PL/pgSQL function ingest_tick(text,text,timestamp with time zone,numeric,numeric,text,text) line 8 at SQL statement
<<< actual SQLSTATE: 42501
ROLLBACK TO SAVEPOINT f;
RESET ROLE;
what the allowed actions changed inside the transaction:
SELECT rule_id, cooldown_seconds, is_active FROM alert_rules WHERE rule_id IN (3, 4) ORDER BY rule_id;
 rule_id | cooldown_seconds | is_active 
---------+------------------+-----------
       3 |               60 | f
       4 |               45 | t
(2 rows)

